# chown Command (Change Owner)

`chown` is used to change the **owner** of a file or directory.

---

## Basic Syntax

```bash
chown user file

###Examples

sudo chown elif notes.txt
  
sudo chown user:group file
sudo chown elif:developers script.sh

sudo chown :group file
sudo chown :developers project.txt

sudo chown -R user:group foldername
sudo chown -R elif:developers myfolder


